            <ArticleTitle>Platelets and antiplatelet therapy in patients with diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>264-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atherosclerotic heart disease is the leading cause of death in patients with diabetes mellitus. Platelets play a major role in the clinical manifestations of ischemic heart disease. Diabetic patients have hyperreactive platelets with exaggerated adhesion, aggregation and thrombin generation. Antiplatelet agents, including aspirin, clopidogrel, and glycoprotein IIb/IIIa inhibitors, have shown significant efficacy in reducing recurrent ischemic events in patients with diabetes. Treatment with glycoprotein IIb/IIIa inhibitors during percutaneous coronary intervention reduces mortality in diabetic patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
